# Categorize manifests as text. Allows automated formatting to handle line endings in a consistent manner.
*.json text

# Force lf line endings on index for files categorized as text
text eol=lf
# Patch files must check out LF on every platform, or vcpkg's PATCHES step fails
# against LF sources and reports it as a corrupt patch rather than a line-ending
# problem. `-text` disables conversion entirely, so the LF bytes in the index are
# the bytes on disk regardless of the cloner's core.autocrlf.
#
# The `text eol=lf` line above does NOT do this: `text` there is a *pattern*, so it
# matches a file literally named `text` and nothing else. Verified with
# `git check-attr text eol -- ports/greenlet/patches/delete_setup_py.patch`, which
# returns `unspecified` for both. Left in place rather than widened to `* text=auto`,
# which would renormalize the whole registry.
*.patch -text
